{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-343110" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the Laplace transform $Y(s)=L{y(t)}$ for $s>2$ if \n\n$$\n{y}^{′}-2y=5-2{e}^{-t},\\,y(0)=\\frac{1}{3}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072504/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c9de028011f1e83dbb0ef31f4ce346d35151d403e6876dfcf3a0e2aba9093fb"} {"question" "q-343110" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we take the Laplace transform of both sides and use the addition and scalar multiplication properties of the Laplace transform:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{y}^{′}-2y} & =L{5-2{e}^{-t}} \\\\ L{{y}^{′}}-2L{y} & =5L{1}-2L{{e}^{-t}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate $L{{y}^{′}},$ we use the formula for the Laplace transform of a derivative and the initial condition $y(0)=\\frac{1}{3}:$\n\n$$\nL{{y}^{′}}=sY(s)-y(0)=sY(s)-\\frac{1}{3}\n$$\n\nFrom the table of Laplace transforms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{t}^{n}} & =\\frac{n!}{{s}^{n+1}},\\,s>0,\\,n\\in {N}_{0} \\\\ L{{e}^{at}} & =\\frac{1}{s-a},\\,s>a\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have the following results:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{1} & =\\frac{1}{s} \\\\ L{{e}^{-t}} & =\\frac{1}{s-(-1)}=\\frac{1}{s+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{y}^{′}}-2L{y} & =5L{1}-2L{{e}^{-t}} \\\\ (sY(s)-\\frac{1}{3})-2Y(s) & =\\frac{5}{s}-\\frac{2}{s+1} \\\\ (s-2)Y(s) & =\\frac{1}{3}+\\frac{5}{s}-\\frac{2}{s+1} \\\\ (s-2)Y(s) & =\\frac{s(s+1)+15(s+1)-6s}{3s(s+1)} \\\\ Y(s) & =\\frac{{s}^{2}+10s+15}{3s(s+1)(s-2)}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072504/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c9de028011f1e83dbb0ef31f4ce346d35151d403e6876dfcf3a0e2aba9093fb"} {"question" "q-343110" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072504/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "582c2f0bd0ab032eb7c8309378b330eee461f89dd791e2b7db3c90ff8030330c"} {"question" "q-343110" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072504/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c9de028011f1e83dbb0ef31f4ce346d35151d403e6876dfcf3a0e2aba9093fb"} {"question" "q-343110" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "Y(s)=\\frac{{s}^{2}+10s+12}{3s(s+1)(s-2)}"] ["math" "Y(s)=\\frac{{s}^{2}+10s+15}{3s(s+1)(s+2)}"] ["math" "Y(s)=\\frac{{s}^{2}+10s+15}{3s(s+1)(s-2)}"] ["math" "Y(s)=\\frac{{s}^{2}+8s+12}{3s(s+1)(s-2)}"] ["math" "Y(s)=\\frac{{s}^{2}+8s+15}{3s(s-1)(s-2)}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072504/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c9de028011f1e83dbb0ef31f4ce346d35151d403e6876dfcf3a0e2aba9093fb"} {"question" "q-343110" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "Y(s)=\\frac{{s}^{2}+10s+15}{3s(s+1)(s-2)}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072504/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c9de028011f1e83dbb0ef31f4ce346d35151d403e6876dfcf3a0e2aba9093fb"} {"question" "q-342871" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the Laplace transform $Y(s)=L{y(t)}$ for $s>2$ if \n\n$$\n{y}^{′}-2y=-5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,y(0)=1.\n$$\n\nYou may make use of the following result:\n\n$$\nL{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\omega t}=\\frac{\\omega }{{s}^{2}+{\\omega }^{2}},\\,s>0.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072504/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c9de028011f1e83dbb0ef31f4ce346d35151d403e6876dfcf3a0e2aba9093fb"} {"question" "q-342871" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we take the Laplace transform of both sides and use the addition and scalar multiplication properties of the Laplace transform:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{y}^{′}-2y} & =L{-5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t} \\\\ L{{y}^{′}}-2L{y} & =-5L{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate $L{{y}^{′}},$ we use the formula for the Laplace transform of a derivative and the initial condition $y(0)=1:$\n\n$$\nL{{y}^{′}}=sL{y}-y(0)=sY(s)-1\n$$\n\nFrom the table of Laplace transforms, we have the following result:\n\n$$\nL{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}=\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}+1},\\,s>0\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can solve for $Y(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{y}^{′}}-2L{y} & =-5L{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t} \\\\ (sY(s)-1)-2Y(s) & =-5(\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}+1}) \\\\ sY(s)-2Y(s) & =1-\\frac{5}{{s}^{2}+1} \\\\ (s-2)Y(s) & =\\frac{{s}^{2}-4}{{s}^{2}+1} \\\\ Y(s) & =\\frac{{s}^{2}-4}{({s}^{2}+1)(s-2)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $s>2,$ we simplify as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Y(s) & =\\frac{(s-2)(s+2)}{({s}^{2}+1)(s-2)} \\\\ Y(s) & =\\frac{s+2}{{s}^{2}+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072504/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c9de028011f1e83dbb0ef31f4ce346d35151d403e6876dfcf3a0e2aba9093fb"} {"question" "q-342871" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072504/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "582c2f0bd0ab032eb7c8309378b330eee461f89dd791e2b7db3c90ff8030330c"} {"question" "q-342871" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072504/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c9de028011f1e83dbb0ef31f4ce346d35151d403e6876dfcf3a0e2aba9093fb"} {"question" "q-342871" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "Y(s)=\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}+1}"] ["math" "Y(s)=\\frac{s+2}{({s}^{2}+1)(s-2)}"] ["math" "Y(s)=\\frac{s+2}{{s}^{2}+1}"] ["math" "Y(s)=\\frac{s-2}{{s}^{2}+1}"] ["math" "Y(s)=\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+1}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072504/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c9de028011f1e83dbb0ef31f4ce346d35151d403e6876dfcf3a0e2aba9093fb"} {"question" "q-342871" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "Y(s)=\\frac{s+2}{{s}^{2}+1}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072504/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c9de028011f1e83dbb0ef31f4ce346d35151d403e6876dfcf3a0e2aba9093fb"} {"question" "q-64482" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the Laplace transform $Y(s)=L{y(t)}$ for $s>0$ if\n\n$$\n2{y}^{′}+2y=4+{t}^{2},\\,y(0)=0.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072504/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c9de028011f1e83dbb0ef31f4ce346d35151d403e6876dfcf3a0e2aba9093fb"} {"question" "q-64482" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we take the Laplace transform of both sides and use the addition and scalar multiplication properties of the Laplace transform:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{2{y}^{′}+2y} & =L{4+{t}^{2}} \\\\ 2L{{y}^{′}}+2L{y} & =4L{1}+L{{t}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate $L{{y}^{′}},$ we use the formula for the Laplace transform of a derivative and the initial condition $y(0)=0:$\n\n$$\nL{{y}^{′}}=sY(s)-y(0)=sY(s)\n$$\n\nFrom the table of Laplace transforms:\n\n$$\nL{{t}^{n}}=\\frac{n!}{{s}^{n+1}},\\,s>0,\\,n\\in {N}_{0}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have the following results:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{1} & =\\frac{1}{s} \\\\ L{{t}^{2}} & =\\frac{2}{{s}^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2L{{y}^{′}}+2L{y} & =4L{1}+L{{t}^{2}} \\\\ 2sY(s)+2Y(s) & =4\\cdot \\frac{1}{s}+\\frac{2}{{s}^{3}} \\\\ (2s+2)Y(s) & =\\frac{4{s}^{2}+2}{{s}^{3}} \\\\ Y(s) & =\\frac{2(2{s}^{2}+1)}{{s}^{3}(2s+2)} \\\\ Y(s) & =\\frac{2{s}^{2}+1}{{s}^{3}(s+1)}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072504/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c9de028011f1e83dbb0ef31f4ce346d35151d403e6876dfcf3a0e2aba9093fb"} {"question" "q-64482" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072504/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "582c2f0bd0ab032eb7c8309378b330eee461f89dd791e2b7db3c90ff8030330c"} {"question" "q-64482" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072504/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c9de028011f1e83dbb0ef31f4ce346d35151d403e6876dfcf3a0e2aba9093fb"} {"question" "q-64482" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "Y(s)=\\frac{2{s}^{2}+1}{{s}^{3}(s+1)}"] ["math" "Y(s)=\\frac{4s+1}{2{s}^{3}(s+1)}"] ["math" "Y(s)=\\frac{4{s}^{2}+1}{4s(s+1)}"] ["math" "Y(s)=\\frac{s+2}{s(s+1)}"] ["math" "Y(s)=\\frac{{s}^{2}-2}{{s}^{3}(s+1)}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072504/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c9de028011f1e83dbb0ef31f4ce346d35151d403e6876dfcf3a0e2aba9093fb"} {"question" "q-64482" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "Y(s)=\\frac{2{s}^{2}+1}{{s}^{3}(s+1)}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072504/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c9de028011f1e83dbb0ef31f4ce346d35151d403e6876dfcf3a0e2aba9093fb"} {"question" "q-342473" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the Laplace transform $Y(s)=L{y(t)}$ for $s>3$ if \n\n$$\n{y}^{′}+y=-8\\operatorname{cosh}⁡3t,\\,y(0)=1.\n$$\n\nYou may make use of the following result:\n\n$$\nL{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡\\omega t}=\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}-{\\omega }^{2}},\\,s>|\\omega |.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072504/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c9de028011f1e83dbb0ef31f4ce346d35151d403e6876dfcf3a0e2aba9093fb"} {"question" "q-342473" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we take the Laplace transform of both sides and use the addition and scalar multiplication properties of the Laplace transform:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{y}^{′}+y} & =L{-8\\operatorname{cosh}⁡3t} \\\\ L{{y}^{′}}+L{y} & =-8L{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡3t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate $L{{y}^{′}},$ we use the formula for the Laplace transform of a derivative and the initial condition $y(0)=1:$\n\n$$\nL{{y}^{′}}=sL{y}-y(0)=sY(s)-1\n$$\n\nFrom the table of Laplace transforms, we have the following result:\n\n$$\nL{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡3t}=\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}-9},\\,s>3\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can solve for $Y(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{y}^{′}}+L{y} & =-8L{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡3t} \\\\ (sY(s)-1)+Y(s) & =-8(\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}-9}) \\\\ sY(s)+Y(s) & =1-\\frac{8s}{{s}^{2}-9} \\\\ (s+1)Y(s) & =\\frac{{s}^{2}-8s-9}{{s}^{2}-9} \\\\ Y(s) & =\\frac{{s}^{2}-8s-9}{({s}^{2}-9)(s+1)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $s>3,$ we simplify as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Y(s) & =\\frac{({s}^{2}-8s-9)}{({s}^{2}-9)(s+1)} \\\\ Y(s) & =\\frac{(s-9)(s+1)}{({s}^{2}-9)(s+1)} \\\\ Y(s) & =\\frac{s-9}{{s}^{2}-9}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072504/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c9de028011f1e83dbb0ef31f4ce346d35151d403e6876dfcf3a0e2aba9093fb"} {"question" "q-342473" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072504/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "582c2f0bd0ab032eb7c8309378b330eee461f89dd791e2b7db3c90ff8030330c"} {"question" "q-342473" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072504/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c9de028011f1e83dbb0ef31f4ce346d35151d403e6876dfcf3a0e2aba9093fb"} {"question" "q-342473" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "Y(s)=\\frac{s+9}{{s}^{2}-9}"] ["math" "Y(s)=\\frac{s-9}{{s}^{2}+9}"] ["math" "Y(s)=\\frac{s-9}{{s}^{2}-9}"] ["math" "Y(s)=\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+9}"] ["math" "Y(s)=\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}-9}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072504/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c9de028011f1e83dbb0ef31f4ce346d35151d403e6876dfcf3a0e2aba9093fb"} {"question" "q-342473" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "Y(s)=\\frac{s-9}{{s}^{2}-9}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072504/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c9de028011f1e83dbb0ef31f4ce346d35151d403e6876dfcf3a0e2aba9093fb"} {"question" "q-64480" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the Laplace transform $Y(s)=L{y(t)}$ for $s>0$ if\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}+4y=2+t,\\,y(0)=3.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072504/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c9de028011f1e83dbb0ef31f4ce346d35151d403e6876dfcf3a0e2aba9093fb"} {"question" "q-64480" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we take the Laplace transform of both sides and use the addition and scalar multiplication properties of the Laplace transform:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{y}^{′}+4y} & =L{2+t} \\\\ L{{y}^{′}}+4L{y} & =2L{1}+L{t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate $L{{y}^{′}},$ we use the formula for the Laplace transform of a derivative and the initial condition $y(0)=3:$\n\n$$\nL{{y}^{′}}=sY(s)-y(0)=sY(s)-3\n$$\n\nFrom the table of Laplace transforms:\n\n$$\nL{{t}^{n}}=\\frac{n!}{{s}^{n+1}},\\,s>0,\\,n\\in {N}_{0}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have the following results:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{1} & =\\frac{1}{s} \\\\ L{t} & =\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{y}^{′}}+4L{y} & =2L{1}+L{t} \\\\ (sY(s)-3)+4Y(s) & =2\\cdot \\frac{1}{s}+\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}} \\\\ sY(s)+4Y(s) & =3+\\frac{2}{s}+\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}} \\\\ (s+4)Y(s) & =\\frac{3{s}^{2}+2s+1}{{s}^{2}} \\\\ Y(s) & =\\frac{3{s}^{2}+2s+1}{{s}^{2}(s+4)}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072504/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c9de028011f1e83dbb0ef31f4ce346d35151d403e6876dfcf3a0e2aba9093fb"} {"question" "q-64480" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072504/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "582c2f0bd0ab032eb7c8309378b330eee461f89dd791e2b7db3c90ff8030330c"} {"question" "q-64480" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072504/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c9de028011f1e83dbb0ef31f4ce346d35151d403e6876dfcf3a0e2aba9093fb"} {"question" "q-64480" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "Y(s)=\\frac{-{s}^{2}+1}{{s}^{2}(s+4)},\\,s>0"] ["math" "Y(s)=\\frac{2{s}^{2}+1}{s(s+4)},\\,s>0"] ["math" "Y(s)=\\frac{3{s}^{2}+2s+1}{{s}^{2}(s+4)},\\,s>0"] ["math" "Y(s)=\\frac{5{s}^{2}+1}{{s}^{3}(s+4)},\\,s>0"] ["math" "Y(s)=\\frac{s-3}{s+4},\\,s>0"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072504/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c9de028011f1e83dbb0ef31f4ce346d35151d403e6876dfcf3a0e2aba9093fb"} {"question" "q-64480" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "Y(s)=\\frac{3{s}^{2}+2s+1}{{s}^{2}(s+4)},\\,s>0"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072504/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c9de028011f1e83dbb0ef31f4ce346d35151d403e6876dfcf3a0e2aba9093fb"} {"question" "q-342499" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following initial value problem.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}+5y=9{e}^{3t},\\,y(0)=0\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options in the reasoning below to find the solution using Laplace transforms.\n\nLet $Y(s)=L{y(t)}.$ Taking the Laplace transform of both sides of the equation and solving for $Y,$ we have\n\n$$\nY(s)={{field-1}}.\n$$\n\nThe partial fraction decomposition of $Y$ is\n\n$$\nY(s)={{field-2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny(t)={{field-3}}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072504/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c9de028011f1e83dbb0ef31f4ce346d35151d403e6876dfcf3a0e2aba9093fb"} {"question" "q-342499" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we take the Laplace transform of both sides of the differential equation. Using the linearity property, we have\n\n$$\nL{{y}^{′}}+5L{y}=L{9{e}^{3t}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for the transform of a derivative, $L{{y}^{′}}=sY(s)-y(0),$ and the standard transform \n\n$$\nL{{e}^{at}}=\\frac{1}{s-a},\\,s>a,\n$$\n\n \nwe substitute the known values.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}sY(s)-0+5Y(s) & =9\\cdot \\frac{1}{s-3} \\\\ (s+5)Y(s) & =\\frac{9}{s-3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving for $Y(s),$ we have\n\n$$\nY(s)=\\frac{9}{(s-3)(s+5)}.\n$$\n\nNext, we perform a partial fraction decomposition. We write $Y(s)$ in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{9}{(s-3)(s+5)}=\\frac{A}{s-3}+\\frac{B}{s+5}.\n$$\n\nTo find the constants $A$ and $B,$ we first clear the denominators:\n\n$$\n9=A(s+5)+B(s-3)\n$$\n\nNow, we find the constants $A$ and $B.$\n\n- Setting $s=3,$ we have\n\n$$\n9=A(3+5)+B(0)\\,⟹\\,9=8A\\,⟹\\,A=\\frac{9}{8}.\n$$\n\n- Setting $s=-5,$ we have\n\n$$\n9=A(0)+B(-5-3)\\,⟹\\,9=-8B\\,⟹\\,B=-\\frac{9}{8}.\n$$\n\nThus, the decomposition is\n\n$$\nY(s)=\\frac{9}{8(s-3)}-\\frac{9}{8(s+5)}.\n$$\n\nFrom the table of Laplace transforms, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-3}} & ={e}^{3t} \\\\ {L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+5}} & ={e}^{-5t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, taking the inverse Laplace transform of $Y(s),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(t) & =\\frac{9}{8}{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-3}}-\\frac{9}{8}{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+5}} \\\\ y(t) & =\\frac{9}{8}{e}^{3t}-\\frac{9}{8}{e}^{-5t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072504/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c9de028011f1e83dbb0ef31f4ce346d35151d403e6876dfcf3a0e2aba9093fb"} {"question" "q-342499" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072504/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "582c2f0bd0ab032eb7c8309378b330eee461f89dd791e2b7db3c90ff8030330c"} {"question" "q-342499" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072504/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c9de028011f1e83dbb0ef31f4ce346d35151d403e6876dfcf3a0e2aba9093fb"} {"question" "q-342499" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{(s-3)(s+9)}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{(s-9)(s+5)}"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{(s-3)(s+9)}"] ["math" "\\frac{9}{(s-3)(s+5)}"] ["math" "\\frac{9}{(s-5)(s+3)}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072504/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c9de028011f1e83dbb0ef31f4ce346d35151d403e6876dfcf3a0e2aba9093fb"} {"question" "q-342499" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{9}{(s-3)(s+5)}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072504/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c9de028011f1e83dbb0ef31f4ce346d35151d403e6876dfcf3a0e2aba9093fb"} {"question" "q-342499" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072504/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c9de028011f1e83dbb0ef31f4ce346d35151d403e6876dfcf3a0e2aba9093fb"} {"question" "q-342499" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{9}{4(s-3)}+\\frac{9}{4(s+5)}"] ["math" "-\\frac{9}{8(s-3)}+\\frac{9}{8(s+5)}"] ["math" "\\frac{9}{4(s-3)}-\\frac{9}{4(s+5)}"] ["math" "\\frac{9}{8(s-3)}-\\frac{9}{8(s+5)}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072504/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c9de028011f1e83dbb0ef31f4ce346d35151d403e6876dfcf3a0e2aba9093fb"} {"question" "q-342499" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{9}{8(s-3)}-\\frac{9}{8(s+5)}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072504/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c9de028011f1e83dbb0ef31f4ce346d35151d403e6876dfcf3a0e2aba9093fb"} {"question" "q-342499" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072504/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c9de028011f1e83dbb0ef31f4ce346d35151d403e6876dfcf3a0e2aba9093fb"} {"question" "q-342499" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{9}{8}{e}^{-3t}+\\frac{9}{8}{e}^{5t}"] ["math" "-\\frac{9}{8}{e}^{3t}+\\frac{9}{8}{e}^{-5t}"] ["math" "\\frac{9}{8}{e}^{-3t}-\\frac{9}{8}{e}^{5t}"] ["math" "\\frac{9}{8}{e}^{3t}-\\frac{9}{8}{e}^{-5t}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072504/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c9de028011f1e83dbb0ef31f4ce346d35151d403e6876dfcf3a0e2aba9093fb"} {"question" "q-342499" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{9}{8}{e}^{3t}-\\frac{9}{8}{e}^{-5t}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072504/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c9de028011f1e83dbb0ef31f4ce346d35151d403e6876dfcf3a0e2aba9093fb"} {"question" "q-342501" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following initial value problem.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}+3y=4{e}^{t},\\,y(0)=0\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options in the reasoning below to find the solution using Laplace transforms.\n\nLet $Y(s)=L{y(t)}.$ Taking the Laplace transform of both sides of the equation and solving for $Y,$ we have\n\n$$\nY(s)={{field-1}}.\n$$\n\nThe partial fraction decomposition of $Y$ is\n\n$$\nY(s)={{field-2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny(t)={{field-3}}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072504/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c9de028011f1e83dbb0ef31f4ce346d35151d403e6876dfcf3a0e2aba9093fb"} {"question" "q-342501" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we take the Laplace transform of both sides of the differential equation. Using the linearity property, we have\n\n$$\nL{{y}^{′}}+3L{y}=L{4{e}^{t}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for the transform of a derivative, $L{{y}^{′}}=sY(s)-y(0),$ and the standard transform \n\n$$\nL{{e}^{at}}=\\frac{1}{s-a},\\,s>a,\n$$\n\n \nwe substitute the known values.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}sY(s)-0+3Y(s) & =4\\cdot \\frac{1}{s-1} \\\\ (s+3)Y(s) & =\\frac{4}{s-1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving for $Y(s),$ we have\n\n$$\nY(s)=\\frac{4}{(s-1)(s+3)}.\n$$\n\nNext, we perform a partial fraction decomposition. We write $Y(s)$ in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{4}{(s-1)(s+3)}=\\frac{A}{s-1}+\\frac{B}{s+3}.\n$$\n\nTo find the constants $A$ and $B,$ we first clear the denominators:\n\n$$\n4=A(s+3)+B(s-1)\n$$\n\nNow, we find the constants $A$ and $B.$\n\n- Setting $s=1,$ we have\n\n$$\n4=A(1+3)+B(0)\\,⟹\\,4=4A\\,⟹\\,A=1.\n$$\n\n- Setting $s=-3,$ we have\n\n$$\n4=A(0)+B(-3-1)\\,⟹\\,4=-4B\\,⟹\\,B=-1.\n$$\n\nThus, the decomposition is\n\n$$\nY(s)=\\frac{1}{s-1}-\\frac{1}{s+3}.\n$$\n\nFrom the table of Laplace transforms, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-1}} & ={e}^{t} \\\\ {L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+3}} & ={e}^{-3t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, taking the inverse Laplace transform of $Y(s),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(t) & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-1}}-{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+3}} \\\\ y(t) & ={e}^{t}-{e}^{-3t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072504/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c9de028011f1e83dbb0ef31f4ce346d35151d403e6876dfcf3a0e2aba9093fb"} {"question" "q-342501" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072504/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "582c2f0bd0ab032eb7c8309378b330eee461f89dd791e2b7db3c90ff8030330c"} {"question" "q-342501" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072504/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c9de028011f1e83dbb0ef31f4ce346d35151d403e6876dfcf3a0e2aba9093fb"} {"question" "q-342501" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{(s-4)(s+1)}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{(s-4)(s+3)}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{(s-1)(s+4)}"] ["math" "\\frac{4}{(s-1)(s+3)}"] ["math" "\\frac{4}{(s-3)(s+1)}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072504/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c9de028011f1e83dbb0ef31f4ce346d35151d403e6876dfcf3a0e2aba9093fb"} {"question" "q-342501" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{4}{(s-1)(s+3)}"] "category" "ma_explicit_answer" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072504/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c9de028011f1e83dbb0ef31f4ce346d35151d403e6876dfcf3a0e2aba9093fb"} {"question" "q-342501" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072504/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c9de028011f1e83dbb0ef31f4ce346d35151d403e6876dfcf3a0e2aba9093fb"} {"question" "q-342501" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{1}{s-1}+\\frac{1}{s+3}"] ["math" "-\\frac{2}{s-1}+\\frac{2}{s+3}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{s-1}-\\frac{1}{s+3}"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{s-1}-\\frac{2}{s+3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072504/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c9de028011f1e83dbb0ef31f4ce346d35151d403e6876dfcf3a0e2aba9093fb"} {"question" "q-342501" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{s-1}-\\frac{1}{s+3}"] "category" "ma_explicit_answer" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072504/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c9de028011f1e83dbb0ef31f4ce346d35151d403e6876dfcf3a0e2aba9093fb"} {"question" "q-342501" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072504/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c9de028011f1e83dbb0ef31f4ce346d35151d403e6876dfcf3a0e2aba9093fb"} {"question" "q-342501" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-{e}^{-t}+{e}^{3t}"] ["math" "-{e}^{t}+{e}^{-3t}"] ["math" "{e}^{-t}-{e}^{3t}"] ["math" "{e}^{t}-{e}^{-3t}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072504/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c9de028011f1e83dbb0ef31f4ce346d35151d403e6876dfcf3a0e2aba9093fb"} {"question" "q-342501" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{e}^{t}-{e}^{-3t}"] "category" "ma_explicit_answer" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072504/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c9de028011f1e83dbb0ef31f4ce346d35151d403e6876dfcf3a0e2aba9093fb"} {"question" "q-342704" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following initial value problem.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}+y=2t+4,\\,y(0)=0\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options in the reasoning below to find the solution using Laplace transforms. You may make use of the following result:\n\n$$\nL{{t}^{n}}=\\frac{n!}{{s}^{n+1}},\\,s>0,\\,n\\in {N}_{0}\n$$\n\nLet $Y(s)=L{y(t)}.$ Taking the Laplace transform of both sides of the equation and solving for $Y,$ we have\n\n$$\nY(s)={{field-1}}.\n$$\n\nThe partial fraction decomposition of $Y$ is\n\n$$\nY(s)={{field-2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny(t)={{field-3}}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072504/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c9de028011f1e83dbb0ef31f4ce346d35151d403e6876dfcf3a0e2aba9093fb"} {"question" "q-342704" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we take the Laplace transform of both sides of the differential equation. Using the linearity property, we have\n\n$$\nL{{y}^{′}}+L{y}=2L{t}+4L{1}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for the transform of a derivative $L{{y}^{′}}=sY(s)-y(0)$ and the standard polynomial transforms\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{t} & =\\frac{1!}{{s}^{1+1}}=\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}}, \\\\ L{1} & =\\frac{0!}{{s}^{0+1}}=\\frac{1}{s},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe substitute the known values. Note that $y(0)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(sY(s)-0)+Y(s) & =2\\cdot \\frac{1}{{s}^{2}}+4\\cdot \\frac{1}{s} \\\\ (s+1)Y(s) & =\\frac{2}{{s}^{2}}+\\frac{4}{s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe rearrange to solve for $Y(s).$ First, find a common denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(s+1)Y(s) & =\\frac{2}{{s}^{2}}+\\frac{4s}{{s}^{2}} \\\\ (s+1)Y(s) & =\\frac{4s+2}{{s}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDividing by $(s+1),$ we obtain\n\n$$\nY(s)=\\frac{4s+2}{{s}^{2}(s+1)}.\n$$\n\nNext, we perform a partial fraction decomposition. Since the denominator has a linear factor $(s+1)$ and a repeated linear factor ${s}^{2},$ we write\n\n$$\n\\frac{4s+2}{{s}^{2}(s+1)}=\\frac{A}{s}+\\frac{B}{{s}^{2}}+\\frac{C}{s+1}.\n$$\n\nTo find the constants, we clear the denominators:\n\n$$\n4s+2=As(s+1)+B(s+1)+C{s}^{2}\n$$\n\n- Setting $s=-1,$ we have\n \n\n$$\n4(-1)+2=A(0)+B(0)+C(-1)^{2}\\,⟹\\,-2=C\\,⟹\\,C=-2.\n$$\n\n- Setting $s=0,$ we have\n  \n\n$$\n4(0)+2=A(0)+B(0+1)+C(0)\\,⟹\\,2=B\\,⟹\\,B=2.\n$$\n\n- Comparing the coefficients of $s,$ we have\n \n\n$$\n4=A+B\\,⟹\\,4=A+2\\,⟹\\,A=2.\n$$\n\nThus, the decomposition is\n\n$$\nY(s)=\\frac{2}{s}+\\frac{2}{{s}^{2}}-\\frac{2}{s+1}.\n$$\n\nFrom the table of Laplace transforms, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s}} & =1 \\\\ {L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}}} & =t \\\\ {L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+1}} & ={e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, taking the inverse Laplace transform of $Y(s),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(t) & =2{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s}}+2{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}}}-2{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+1}} \\\\ y(t) & =2+2t-2{e}^{-t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072504/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c9de028011f1e83dbb0ef31f4ce346d35151d403e6876dfcf3a0e2aba9093fb"} {"question" "q-342704" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072504/activity-metadata.json" "