/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072504/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c9de028011f1e83dbb0ef31f4ce346d35151d403e6876dfcf3a0e2aba9093fb"} {"question" "q-342704" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{2}{s}+\\frac{2}{{s}^{2}}-\\frac{2}{s+1}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072504/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c9de028011f1e83dbb0ef31f4ce346d35151d403e6876dfcf3a0e2aba9093fb"} {"question" "q-342704" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072504/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c9de028011f1e83dbb0ef31f4ce346d35151d403e6876dfcf3a0e2aba9093fb"} {"question" "q-342704" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2+2t+2{e}^{-t}"] ["math" "-2-2t+2{e}^{-t}"] ["math" "2+2t-2{e}^{-t}"] ["math" "2-2t-2{e}^{-t}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072504/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c9de028011f1e83dbb0ef31f4ce346d35151d403e6876dfcf3a0e2aba9093fb"} {"question" "q-342704" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2+2t-2{e}^{-t}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072504/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c9de028011f1e83dbb0ef31f4ce346d35151d403e6876dfcf3a0e2aba9093fb"} {"question" "q-342928" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following initial value problem.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}+3y=4{e}^{-2t},\\,y(0)=2\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options in the reasoning below to find the solution using Laplace transforms.\n\nLet $Y(s)=L{y(t)}.$ Taking the Laplace transform of both sides of the equation and solving for $Y,$ we have\n\n$$\nY(s)={{field-1}}.\n$$\n\nThe partial fraction decomposition of $Y$ is\n\n$$\nY(s)={{field-2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny(t)={{field-3}}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072504/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c9de028011f1e83dbb0ef31f4ce346d35151d403e6876dfcf3a0e2aba9093fb"} {"question" "q-342928" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we take the Laplace transform of both sides of the differential equation. Using the linearity property, we have\n\n$$\nL{{y}^{′}}+3L{y}=L{4{e}^{-2t}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for the transform of a derivative, $L{{y}^{′}}=sY(s)-y(0),$ and the standard transform \n\n$$\nL{{e}^{at}}=\\frac{1}{s-a},\\,s>a,\n$$\n\nwe substitute the known values. Note that $y(0)=2:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(sY(s)-2)+3Y(s) & =4\\cdot \\frac{1}{s+2} \\\\ (s+3)Y(s)-2 & =\\frac{4}{s+2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe rearrange to solve for $Y(s).$ First, add $2$ to the right-hand side and find a common denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(s+3)Y(s) & =2+\\frac{4}{s+2} \\\\ (s+3)Y(s) & =\\frac{2(s+2)}{s+2}+\\frac{4}{s+2} \\\\ (s+3)Y(s) & =\\frac{2s+8}{s+2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDividing by $(s+3),$ we obtain\n\n$$\nY(s)=\\frac{2s+8}{(s+3)(s+2)}.\n$$\n\nNext, we perform a partial fraction decomposition. We write $Y(s)$ in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{2s+8}{(s+3)(s+2)}=\\frac{A}{s+3}+\\frac{B}{s+2}.\n$$\n\nTo find the constants $A$ and $B,$ we first clear the denominators:\n\n$$\n2s+8=A(s+2)+B(s+3)\n$$\n\nNow, we find the constants $A$ and $B.$\n\n- Setting $s=-3,$ we have\n\n$$\n2(-3)+8=A(-3+2)+B(0)\\,⟹\\,2=-1A\\,⟹\\,A=-2.\n$$\n\n- Setting $s=-2,$ we have\n\n$$\n2(-2)+8=A(0)+B(-2+3)\\,⟹\\,4=1B\\,⟹\\,B=4.\n$$\n\nThus, the decomposition is\n\n$$\nY(s)=-\\frac{2}{s+3}+\\frac{4}{s+2}.\n$$\n\nFrom the table of Laplace transforms, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+3}} & ={e}^{-3t} \\\\ {L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+2}} & ={e}^{-2t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, taking the inverse Laplace transform of $Y(s),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(t) & =-2{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+3}}+4{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+2}} \\\\ y(t) & =-2{e}^{-3t}+4{e}^{-2t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072504/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c9de028011f1e83dbb0ef31f4ce346d35151d403e6876dfcf3a0e2aba9093fb"} {"question" "q-342928" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072504/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "582c2f0bd0ab032eb7c8309378b330eee461f89dd791e2b7db3c90ff8030330c"} {"question" "q-342928" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072504/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c9de028011f1e83dbb0ef31f4ce346d35151d403e6876dfcf3a0e2aba9093fb"} {"question" "q-342928" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{(s+3)(s-2)}"] ["math" "\\frac{2s+4}{(s+3)(s+2)}"] ["math" "\\frac{2s+8}{(s+3)(s+2)}"] ["math" "\\frac{2s}{(s+3)(s+2)}"] ["math" "\\frac{4}{(s+3)(s+2)}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072504/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c9de028011f1e83dbb0ef31f4ce346d35151d403e6876dfcf3a0e2aba9093fb"} {"question" "q-342928" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{2s+8}{(s+3)(s+2)}"] "category" "ma_explicit_answer" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Acad