partial fraction decomposition of $Y$ is\n\n$$\nY(s)={{field-2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny(t)={{field-3}}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072504/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c9de028011f1e83dbb0ef31f4ce346d35151d403e6876dfcf3a0e2aba9093fb"} {"question" "q-343063" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we take the Laplace transform of both sides of the differential equation. Using the linearity property, we have\n\n$$\nL{{y}^{′}}+3L{y}=2L{\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t}-3L{\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for the transform of a derivative $L{{y}^{′}}=sY(s)-y(0)$ and the standard trigonometric transforms\n\n$$\nL{\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t}=\\frac{2}{{s}^{2}+4},\\,L{\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t}=\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+4},\n$$\n\nwe substitute the known values. Note that $y(0)=-2:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(sY(s)-(-2))+3Y(s) & =2(\\frac{2}{{s}^{2}+4})-3(\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+4}) \\\\ (s+3)Y(s)+2 & =\\frac{4-3s}{{s}^{2}+4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe rearrange to solve for $Y(s).$ First, subtract $2$ from the right-hand side and find a common denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(s+3)Y(s) & =\\frac{4-3s}{{s}^{2}+4}-2 \\\\ (s+3)Y(s) & =\\frac{4-3s}{{s}^{2}+4}-\\frac{2({s}^{2}+4)}{{s}^{2}+4} \\\\ (s+3)Y(s) & =\\frac{-2{s}^{2}-3s-4}{{s}^{2}+4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDividing by $(s+3),$ we obtain\n\n$$\nY(s)=\\frac{-2{s}^{2}-3s-4}{(s+3)({s}^{2}+4)}.\n$$\n\nNext, we perform a partial fraction decomposition. Since the denominator has a linear factor $(s+3)$ and an irreducible quadratic factor $({s}^{2}+4),$ we write\n\n$$\n\\frac{-2{s}^{2}-3s-4}{(s+3)({s}^{2}+4)}=\\frac{A}{s+3}+\\frac{Bs+C}{{s}^{2}+4}.\n$$\n\nTo find the constants, we clear the denominators:\n\n$$\n-2{s}^{2}-3s-4=A({s}^{2}+4)+(Bs+C)(s+3)\n$$\n\n- Setting $s=-3,$ we have\n \n\n$$\n-2(-3)^{2}-3(-3)-4=A((-3)^{2}+4)+0\\,⟹\\,-13=13A\\,⟹\\,A=-1.\n$$\n\n- Comparing the coefficients of ${s}^{2},$ we have\n  \n\n$$\n-2=A+B\\,⟹\\,-2=-1+B\\,⟹\\,B=-1.\n$$\n\n- Comparing the constant terms, we have\n \n\n$$\n-4=4A+3C\\,⟹\\,-4=4(-1)+3C\\,⟹\\,C=0.\n$$\n\nThus, the decomposition is\n\n$$\nY(s)=-\\frac{1}{s+3}+\\frac{-s}{{s}^{2}+4}=-\\frac{1}{s+3}-\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+4}.\n$$\n\nFrom the table of Laplace transforms, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+3}} & ={e}^{-3t} \\\\ {L}^{-1}{\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+4}} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, taking the inverse Laplace transform of $Y(s),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(t) & =-{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+3}}-{L}^{-1}{\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+4}} \\\\ y(t) & =-{e}^{-3t}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072504/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c9de028011f1e83dbb0ef31f4ce346d35151d403e6876dfcf3a0e2aba9093fb"} {"question" "q-343063" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072504/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "582c2f0bd0ab032eb7c8309378b330eee461f89dd791e2b7db3c90ff8030330c"} {"question" "q-343063" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072504/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c9de028011f1e83dbb0ef31f4ce346d35151d403e6876dfcf3a0e2aba9093fb"} {"question" "q-343063" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{-2{s}^{2}+3s-4}{(s+3)({s}^{2}+4)}"] ["math" "\\frac{-2{s}^{2}-3s-2}{(s+3)({s}^{2}+4)}"] ["math" "\\frac{-2{s}^{2}-3s-4}{(s+1)({s}^{2}+4)}"] ["math" "\\frac{-2{s}^{2}-3s-4}{(s+3)({s}^{2}+4)}"] ["math" "\\frac{2{s}^{2}-3s-4}{(s+3)({s}^{2}+4)}"]] "category" "ma