apture-workers/differential/14072504/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c9de028011f1e83dbb0ef31f4ce346d35151d403e6876dfcf3a0e2aba9093fb"} {"question" "q-343057" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we take the Laplace transform of both sides of the differential equation. Using the linearity property, we have\n\n$$\nL{{y}^{′}}+L{y}=L{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}+L{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for the transform of a derivative $L{{y}^{′}}=sY(s)-y(0)$ and the standard trigonometric transforms\n\n$$\nL{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}=\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}+1},\\,L{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}=\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+1},\n$$\n\nwe substitute the known values. Note that $y(0)=2:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(sY(s)-2)+Y(s) & =\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}+1}+\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+1} \\\\ (s+1)Y(s)-2 & =\\frac{s+1}{{s}^{2}+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe rearrange to solve for $Y(s).$ First, add $2$ to the right-hand side and find a common denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(s+1)Y(s) & =2+\\frac{s+1}{{s}^{2}+1} \\\\ (s+1)Y(s) & =\\frac{2({s}^{2}+1)}{{s}^{2}+1}+\\frac{s+1}{{s}^{2}+1} \\\\ (s+1)Y(s) & =\\frac{2{s}^{2}+s+3}{{s}^{2}+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDividing by $(s+1),$ we obtain\n\n$$\nY(s)=\\frac{2{s}^{2}+s+3}{(s+1)({s}^{2}+1)}.\n$$\n\nNext, we perform a partial fraction decomposition. Since the denominator has a linear factor $(s+1)$ and an irreducible quadratic factor $({s}^{2}+1),$ we write\n\n$$\n\\frac{2{s}^{2}+s+3}{(s+1)({s}^{2}+1)}=\\frac{A}{s+1}+\\frac{Bs+C}{{s}^{2}+1}.\n$$\n\nTo find the constants, we clear the denominators:\n\n$$\n2{s}^{2}+s+3=A({s}^{2}+1)+(Bs+C)(s+1)\n$$\n\n- Setting $s=-1,$ we have\n \n\n$$\n2(-1)^{2}+(-1)+3=A((-1)^{2}+1)+0\\,⟹\\,4=2A\\,⟹\\,A=2.\n$$\n\n- Comparing the coefficients of ${s}^{2},$ we have\n  \n\n$$\n2=A+B\\,⟹\\,2=2+B\\,⟹\\,B=0.\n$$\n\n- Comparing the constant terms, we have\n \n\n$$\n3=A+C\\,⟹\\,3=2+C\\,⟹\\,C=1.\n$$\n\nThus, the decomposition is\n\n$$\nY(s)=\\frac{2}{s+1}+\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}+1}.\n$$\n\nFrom the table of Laplace transforms, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+1}} & ={e}^{-t} \\\\ {L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}+1}} & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, taking the inverse Laplace transform of $Y(s),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(t) & =2{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+1}}+{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}+1}} \\\\ y(t) & =2{e}^{-t}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072504/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c9de028011f1e83dbb0ef31f4ce346d35151d403e6876dfcf3a0e2aba9093fb"} {"question" "q-343057" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072504/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "582c2f0bd0ab032eb7c8309378b330eee461f89dd791e2b7db3c90ff8030330c"} {"question" "q-343057" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072504/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c9de028011f1e83dbb0ef31f4ce346d35151d403e6876dfcf3a0e2aba9093fb"} {"question" "q-343057" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{2{s}^{2}+3}{(s+1)({s}^{2}+1)}"] ["math" "\\frac{2{s}^{2}+s+2}{(s+1)({s}^{2}+1)}"] ["math" "\\frac{2{s}^{2}+s+3}{(s+1)({s}^{2}+1)}"] ["math" "\\frac{2{s}^{2}-s+3}{(s+1)({s}^{2}+1)}"] ["math" "\\frac{{s}^{2}+s+2}{(s+1)({s}^{2}+1)}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072504/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c9de028011f1e83dbb0ef31f4ce346d35151d403e6876dfcf3a0e2aba9093fb"} {"question" "q-343057" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{2{s}^{2}+s+3}{(s+1)({s}^{2}+1)}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072504/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c9de028011f1e83dbb0ef31f4ce346d35151d403e6876dfcf3a0e2aba9093fb"} {"question" "q-343057" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072504/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c9de028011f1e83dbb0ef31f4ce346d35151d403e6876dfcf3a0e2aba9093fb"} {"question" "q-343057" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{s+1}+\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+1}"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{s+1}+\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}+1}"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{s+1}+\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+1}"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{s+1}-\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}+1}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072504/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c9de028011f1e83dbb0ef31f4ce346d35151d403e6876dfcf3a0e2aba9093fb"} {"question" "q-343057" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{2}{s+1}+\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}+1}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072504/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c9de028011f1e83dbb0ef31f4ce346d35151d403e6876dfcf3a0e2aba9093fb"} {"question" "q-343057" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072504/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c9de028011f1e83dbb0ef31f4ce346d35151d403e6876dfcf3a0e2aba9093fb"} {"question" "q-343057" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2{e}^{-t}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t"] ["math" "2{e}^{-t}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t"] ["math" "2{e}^{-t}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t"] ["math" "{e}^{-t}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072504/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c9de028011f1e83dbb0ef31f4ce346d35151d403e6876dfcf3a0e2aba9093fb"} {"question" "q-343057" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2{e}^{-t}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072504/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c9de028011f1e83dbb0ef31f4ce346d35151d403e6876dfcf3a0e2aba9093fb"} {"question" "q-342962" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following initial value problem.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}+6y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t,\\,y(0)=0\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options in the reasoning below to find the solution using Laplace transforms. You may make use of the following results:\n\n$$\nL{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\omega t}=\\frac{\\omega }{{s}^{2}+{\\omega }^{2}},\\,L{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\omega t}=\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+{\\omega }^{2}},\\,s>0.\n$$\n\nLet $Y(s)=L{y(t)}.$ Taking the Laplace transform of both sides of the equation and solving for $Y,$ we have\n\n$$\nY(s)={{field-1}}.\n$$\n\nThe partial fraction decomposition of $Y$ is\n\n$$\nY(s)={{field-2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny(t)={{field-3}}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072504/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c9de028011f1e83dbb0ef31f4ce346d35151d403e6876dfcf3a0e2aba9093fb"} {"question" "q-342962" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we take the Laplace transform of both sides of the differential equation. Using the linearity property, we have\n\n$$\nL{{y}^{′}}+6L{y}=L{\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t}+L{\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for the transform of a derivative $L{{y}^{′}}=sY(s)-y(0)$ and the standard trigonometric transforms\n\n$$\nL{\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t}=\\frac{3}{{s}^{2}+9},\\,L{\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t}=\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+9},\n$$\n\nwe substitute the known values. Note that $y(0)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(sY(s)-0)+6Y(s) & =\\frac{3}{{s}^{2}+9}+\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+9} \\\\ (s+6)Y(s) & =\\frac{s+3}{{s}^{2}+9}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe rearrange to solve for $Y(s).$ Dividing by $(s+6),$ we obtain\n\n$$\nY(s)=\\frac{s+3}{(s+6)({s}^{2}+9)}.\n$$\n\nNext, we perform a partial fraction decomposition. Since the denominator has a linear factor $(s+6)$ and an irreducible quadratic factor $({s}^{2}+9),$ we write\n\n$$\n\\frac{s+3}{(s+6)({s}^{2}+9)}=\\frac{A}{s+6}+\\frac{Bs+C}{{s}^{2}+9}.\n$$\n\nTo find the constants, we clear the denominators:\n\n$$\ns+3=A({s}^{2}+9)+(Bs+C)(s+6)\n$$\n\n- Setting $s=-6,$ we have\n \n\n$$\n-6+3=A((-6)^{2}+9)+0\\,⟹\\,-3=45A\\,⟹\\,A=-\\frac{1}{15}.\n$$\n\n- Comparing the coefficients of ${s}^{2},$ we have\n  \n\n$$\n0=A+B\\,⟹\\,0=-\\frac{1}{15}+B\\,⟹\\,B=\\frac{1}{15}.\n$$\n\n- Comparing the constant terms, we have\n \n\n$$\n3=9A+6C\\,⟹\\,3=-\\frac{3}{5}+6C\\,⟹\\,C=\\frac{3}{5}.\n$$\n\nThus, the decomposition is\n\n$$\nY(s)=\\frac{(-\\frac{1}{15})}{s+6}+\\frac{(\\frac{1}{15}s+\\frac{3}{5})}{{s}^{2}+9}=-\\frac{1}{15(s+6)}+\\frac{s+9}{15({s}^{2}+9)}.\n$$\n\nFrom the table of Laplace transforms, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+6}} & ={e}^{-6t} \\\\ {L}^{-1}{\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+9}} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t \\\\ {L}^{-1}{\\frac{3}{{s}^{2}+9}} & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, taking the inverse Laplace transform of $Y(s),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(t) & =-\\frac{1}{15}{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+6}}+\\frac{1}{15}{L}^{-1}{\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+9}}+\\frac{1}{5}{L}^{-1}{\\frac{3}{{s}^{2}+9}} \\\\ y(t) & =-\\frac{1}{15}{e}^{-6t}+\\frac{1}{15}\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t+\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072504/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c9de028011f1e83dbb0ef31f4ce346d35151d403e6876dfcf3a0e2aba9093fb"} {"question" "q-342962" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072504/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "582c2f0bd0ab032eb7c8309378b330eee461f89dd791e2b7db3c90ff8030330c"} {"question" "q-342962" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072504/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c9de028011f1e83dbb0ef31f4ce346d35151d403e6876dfcf3a0e2aba9093fb"} {"question" "q-342962" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{3-s}{(s+6)({s}^{2}+9)}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{(s+6)({s}^{2}+9)}"] ["math" "\\frac{s+3}{(s+6)({s}^{2}+9)}"] ["math" "\\frac{s-3}{(s+6)({s}^{2}+9)}"] ["math" "\\frac{s}{(s+6)({s}^{2}+9)}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072504/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c9de028011f1e83dbb0ef31f4ce346d35151d403e6876dfcf3a0e2aba9093fb"} {"question" "q-342962" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{s+3}{(s+6)({s}^{2}+9)}"] "category" "ma_explicit_answer" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072504/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c9de028011f1e83dbb0ef31f4ce346d35151d403e6876dfcf3a0e2aba9093fb"} {"question" "q-342962" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_wid